sk->sk_prot->unhash(sk);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because `sock_release(smc->clcsock)` is called after `sk->sk_prot->unhash(sk)`, which releases the socket but does not unhash it first. This can lead to a use-after-free condition if a parallel operation, such as `smc_diag_dump()`, tries to access `smc->clcsock` after it has been released but before it has been unhashed, resulting in illegal memory access.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
sk->sk_prot->unhash(sk);
sock_release(smc->clcsock);
```
Reason:
The fix moves the `sk->sk_prot->unhash(sk)` statement before `sock_release(smc->clcsock)`. This ensures that the socket is unhashed before it is released, preventing any parallel operations from accessing a freed socket, thus eliminating the potential for a use-after-free condition.


